// A staccato dot sits OPPOSITE the stem. On a tab a BEAMED note follows the
// beam's (group) direction, not its own string: this group spans strings 4 and 2
// with an UP beam, so every dot — including the string-2 notes' — sits BELOW the
// digit, not on the stem side. (Using the per-note string put the string-2 dots
// above, on the stem.)
title "tab staccato on beamed group"
time 4/4
key c major
part m { instrument bass section A { g8@staccato g g'\2@staccato g\2 | } }
form main { A }
score main { tab m }
